troducing  is the fragmentation among the three  emperors they're not exactly cooperating  right now it was really interesting to  see the middle brother chastised the  younger brother for destroying the  planets thespis and enacrion in a  previous episode he points out that it  was reckless impulsive behavior and it's  caused way more problems than it  actually solved  now on that same line one of the most  famous lines in all of asimov's work is  violence is the last refuge of the  incompetent and this is a line that is  first said by mayor hardin i believe but  in the show  things are a bit different the most  important the most famous asimov line is  now just an old man thing according to  the tv show version of hardin this is  one of the changes that i really don't  get why is hardin someone in who in the  books says violence is the last refuge  of the incompetent so quick in the show  to grab a gun it's a change from the  books that at the moment i just don't  really understand but it could be an  opportunity for character development in  the future some other changes from the  book that showed up in this episode was  that harden seems to have mentality  abilities perhaps actually it almost is  certain that harden does have mentality  abilities in the show and basically  mentality abilities give you the ability  to read minds and manipulate people's  thoughts and their minds the problem  with metallic abilities is they kind of  throw off  psycho history psycho history has a hard  time predicting the future when the  variables of mentality abilities are  thrown in so it seems like somebody is  communicating with hardin from the  library on trantor and if you read the  books you know exactly well not exactly  but you have some idea of what's going  on here because there is a very specific  group  that is involved on trantor and i won't  spoil that for people that want to keep  watching the show to find out but there  is some book basis for like her seeing  someone on trantor if she is in fact  metallic which it looks like she  definitely is there was also a scene in  this show when she was flipping coins  and she was guessing the coin flip that  is not  in  the mentality abilities i don't think  from the book so that is like an extra  layer that they're putting on the show  that they somehow have these predictive  powers which i don't think is anywhere  in the books ultimately i found the plot  on terminus involving an acrion  and them trying to get past the fence  and them going to dig a tunnel i found  all of it extraordinarily tedious and  very  seen it all before  i wasn't particularly engaged throughout  any of it and that's sad to say i just  didn't find it particularly interesting  i thought the characters just all seem  pretty generic including the new  enactrion huntress that they've  introduced i just thought she's just  kind of a generic character that i've  seen in a bunch of other places before  harden has still not become any more  interesting to me unfortunately and none  of the other characters on terminus i'm  really care about at all either and  that's really a shame because if they're  going to make the pacing suffer so that  they can keep these characters around  and develop these characters they need  to give the characters traits and  identities that we can relate to and  actually care about when i watch the  character harden in this show i don't  really know what she cares about i don't  really know what her passions are i  don't really know what she even wants  out of life she's just kind of wandering  around reacting to things and to me  that's not a well-written character a  character should be more than just a  blank thing that's reacting to things  that are happening to them judging by  the pacing of the last two episodes my  hope of this show being a show based  around time jumps in any significant way  are kind of becoming a little bit dashed  because i can see them wanting to sit  with these 